# Wave B.a — Denali sync resolve consolidation

## Problem

`apps/web/src/wizard/denali/resolve-sync-workspace-plugin.ts` statically imported `@app-tour/workspace-denali/plugin` for create/flat-edit hooks, **in addition to** the generated draft-shell binding that already exposes `getDenaliWorkspacePluginFromDraftShell` (static host chrome import). The `loadPlugin` callbacks wrapped that sync call in `async` without using the P4.1 allowlisted loader.

## Decision

| API | Implementation |
| --- | -------------- |
| `resolveDenaliSyncWorkspacePlugin()` | Delegate to `getDenaliWorkspacePluginFromDraftShell()` (single static product entry already required by draft-shell codegen) |
| `loadDenaliWorkspacePlugin()` | `loadWorkspacePluginByIdFromRegistry(DENALI_PLUGIN_ID)` — true dynamic import path |

Create/flat-edit hooks use **`loadDenaliWorkspacePlugin`** for `loadPlugin` / gate async paths; sync `useMemo` / initial gate profile may still call the draft-shell sync getter until Wave B.b (async-only gate init).

## Out of scope (Wave B.b+)

- Removing static draft-shell codegen import of denali host chrome
- Neutralizing `resolve-bootstrap-workspace-plugin.client.ts` Map
- Deleting `apps/web/src/wizard/denali/` re-export shims

## Verify

```bash
rg "from \"@app-tour/workspace-denali/plugin\"" apps/web/src/wizard -g '!**/test/**'
pnpm --filter @apps/web exec node --import tsx --test test/wizard-create-boundary.spec.ts test/wizard-host-boundary.spec.ts
```
